patrone-installer (0.1.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * No "Automated with Landscape" on the "Type of installation" page:
    Landscape is Canonical's management service (docs/COMPLIANCE.md,
    item 10).
  * A plain disk beside Windows' partitions, in place of Microsoft's logo.
  * Ubuntu's own slides are out of the app: Patrone's are the ones shown,
    and Ubuntu's carried Ubuntu's mascot and 27 other apps' logos.
  * The Applications page no longer promises a web browser: "Patrone's
    desktop, apps and everyday tools. You choose a web browser the first
    time you need one."
  * The Ubuntu fonts' licence (UFL.txt) and Yaru's icon font's notice are
    beside them in the app.
  * The copyright file says Patrone's pictures in it come from a logo made
    with an AI image generator.

